    { "id": "convert.message", "str": "Every managed file will be converted from %1$s to %2$s.\n\nNotes:\n1. Only the %1$s side is read, so tags of files stored as %2$s will be cleared;\n2. Filename mode really renames files;\n3. A big library takes a while, please be patient." },

    { "id": "about.title", "str": "About TagMeow" },
    { "id": "about.body", "str": "Version: 1.0 (work in progress)\n\nStorage: pick one of two modes — (1) SAF granted folders, or (2) all files access with plain paths. Neither needs other permissions; (2) never opens the system picker.\nIndex: local SQLite (always rebuildable).\nTag library: global type -> tag definitions in app storage.\nImporting merges: it replaces only when this library is empty, otherwise it adds just the missing types and tags.\nProject: https://github.com/kakameow/TagMeow" },
    { "id": "about.no_browser", "str": "No app on this device can open web pages" },
    { "id": "help.body", "str": "TagMeow tag model\n\n· Storage: SAF folders only. Only folders you grant are managed.\n\n· Tag library: global type -> tag definitions with colors. Deleting or renaming changes the library only, never the files.\n\n· A file can store tags in two ways:\n  Filename: inside the name, e.g. file{[tag1,tag2]}.txt\n  Sidecar: in a sibling .tag folder, e.g. dir/.tag/file.txt.json\n\n· Folders always use Sidecar: renaming a folder would break inner paths.\n\n· The default mode only affects writes; reads try the default first, then the other one.\n\n· No index yet? Add a folder in Folders, or tap Rescan in Settings." },
    { "id": "dir.pick_body", "str": "TagMeow does not ask for global file access — it only uses folders you grant.\n\nAfter tapping 'Grant', open a subfolder in the system picker (you can create one) and tap 'Use this folder'.\n\nAndroid refuses these locations; picking one shows 'To protect your privacy, you can not use this folder':\n· storage root (internal storage / SD card)\n· Download\n· Android/data, Android/obb" },
    { "id": "dir.permission_lost", "str": "　·　permission needed" },
    { "id": "editor.delete_type_message", "str": "\"%1$s\" and its tags will be removed from the tag library.\nTags already written into files are kept." },
    { "id": "editor.delete_tag_message", "str": "\"%1$s\" will be removed from the tag library.\nTags already written into files are kept." },

